    "subtitle": "How brave students and people stood up for a fair country.",
    "body": "In 1960, Korea was not free. The leaders were not fair. They cheated in the big vote. Many people were angry.\n\nIn a country with democracy, the people choose their leaders. Every vote must count.\n\nStudents felt this was wrong. They did not stay quiet. On April 19, they walked into the streets. They <mark>raised their voices</mark> for change. Soon many people joined them.\n\nThe crowd was peaceful but very strong. They asked for a fair country. This day is called the April 19 Revolution.\n\nIn the end, the unfair leader had to step down.\n\nGood citizens speak up when things are wrong.",
